# LXDE session autostart for the RitaFrame kiosk.
# Installed as ~/.config/lxsession/LXDE-pi/autostart
#
# The panel and desktop are disabled: they sit *above* the browser in the window
# stacking, so leaving them running covers the frame even when surf is fullscreen.
# They also re-map themselves shortly after login, which undoes any attempt to
# hide them from a script. For a kiosk it is simpler not to start them at all.
#
# Comment them back in if you want a normal desktop to debug in.
#@lxpanel --profile LXDE-pi
#@pcmanfm --desktop --profile LXDE-pi

# Rotate the panel to landscape before anything opens a window.
# (rotate-display.sh also runs from ~/.config/autostart as a second safety net.)
point-rpi

# The Flask app, in a terminal on purpose: if it cannot start, the dependency
# error stays on screen instead of failing invisibly. surffull.sh hides this
# window once the browser is up, and run.sh tees to ~/ritaframe.log.
@lxterminal -e /bin/bash /home/pi/Documents/RitaFrame/run.sh

#@xscreensaver -no-splash

# These two run without a terminal. Launching them via @lxterminal leaves an
# empty shell window parked on top of the fullscreen browser, which is exactly
# what we are trying to avoid.
@/home/pi/Documents/RitaFrame/etc/surf/runsurf.sh
@/home/pi/Documents/RitaFrame/etc/surf/surffull.sh
